{#
  Explore other services — the internal-link block that closes every service
  page.

  It used to be a row of pill "tags" on navy, which sat between the navy FAQ and
  the navy footer and read as one undifferentiated dark run. This is the same
  job (link the other three services, for readers and for internal linking) laid
  out as a split: a white card of link rows on cream, beside a large photograph.
  A light band here also puts a deliberate break between the FAQ above and the
  footer CTA below, which is half of why the old version disappeared.

  THE PHOTOGRAPH FOLLOWS THE POINTER. Each row has a matching shot stacked in
  the media panel; hovering or tab-focusing a row crossfades to it. That is done
  with :has() rather than JavaScript, so the whole thing is a plain list of
  links that happens to have a picture attached. Browsers without :has() simply
  keep showing the resting image, which is the first service's.

  Imagery and one-line descriptions come from site.services, so adding a service
  needs nothing here.
#}

{# The current page's own service is dropped, so this is three rows, and the
   rows and the shots share an index by sitting in the same order. That order is
   NOT numbered any more: these are three alternatives, not three steps, and a
   numeral in front of each one implied a sequence that does not exist. #}
{% set others = [] %}
{% for s in site.services %}{% if s.href != currentService %}{% set _ = others.push(s) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% if others.length %}
<section class="section section--light services-explore" aria-labelledby="explore-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="services-explore__split">

      <div class="services-explore__panel">
        <h2 id="explore-title" class="statement services-explore__title">Explore our other services.</h2>
        <p class="services-explore__lead">Water treatment is only ever part of the picture. Whatever your property needs, it is looked after by the same team.</p>

        <ul class="services-explore__card" role="list">
          {% for s in others %}
          <li class="services-explore__row">
            <a class="services-explore__link" href="{{ s.href }}">
              <span class="services-explore__text">
                <span class="services-explore__name">{{ s.title }}</span>
                {% if s.desc %}<span class="services-explore__desc">{{ s.desc }}</span>{% endif %}
              </span>
              <span class="services-explore__arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>

      {# aria-hidden: the shots are decorative here. Each one names a service
         that is already spelled out in the link beside it, so announcing three
         alternating images would only repeat the list. #}
      <div class="services-explore__media" aria-hidden="true">
        {% for s in others %}
        <img class="services-explore__shot" src="{{ s.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="961">
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
